{"title":"2012 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Bernardo and Silvia play the following game. An integer between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/0/0705411d92671faf1fe5602cfef8f353c7f0f83d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$999$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> inclusive is selected and given to Bernardo. Whenever Bernardo receives a number, he doubles it and passes the result to Silvia. Whenever Silvia receives a number, she adds <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> to it and passes the result to Bernardo. The winner is the last person who produces a number less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the smallest initial number that results in a win for Bernardo. What is the sum of the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/f/3af1025237725763f525a2be317da1aefcf3c13e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 7\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 8\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 9\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 10\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"366\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The last number that Bernardo says has to be between 950 and 999. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/e/fbe4765d87bb99b878cce0677742a35406759c38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\rightarrow 2\\rightarrow 52\\rightarrow 104\\rightarrow 154\\rightarrow 308\\rightarrow 358\\rightarrow 716\\rightarrow 766$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"425\" height=\"13\" /> contains 4 doubling actions. Thus, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/b/babb6205b8510ee62e0828644ef74781542e22dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\rightarrow 2x \\rightarrow 2x+50 \\rightarrow 4x+100 \\rightarrow 4x+150 \\rightarrow 8x+300 \\rightarrow 8x+350 \\rightarrow 16x+700$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"641\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/a/dfa4dcd070dd4eca80d44f4747aa6a186b4a088f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$950&lt;16x+700&lt;1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"189\" height=\"14\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/b/0db19ae496b91d020d585a5f306721fbd24a09c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16x&gt;250 \\implies x \\geq 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"181\" height=\"15\" />. \n</p><p>Because we are looking for the smallest integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/2/1628581d2c8bdf5dfbb9d5fafe360ec1773aaff6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=16$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />. Our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/7/79793b0f12454bdb6e29a754735ce574555acae3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+6=\\boxed{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"85\" height=\"23\" />, which is A.\n</p><p>~minor edits by <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Kevinchen_yay\">KevinChen_Yay</a>\n</p><p>~removed unnecessary last step (EvanDu168)\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Work backwards. The last number Bernardo produces must be in the range <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/e/68e9cad028df7dec5e91c9b17f4adbbd69ff997f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[950,999]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />. That means that before this, Silvia must produce a number in the range <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54c7141f734f081bb6dcfec5767313dfefb9eb26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[475,499]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />. Before this, Bernardo must produce a number in the range <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/d/fedca09904c2f859f7cc67a16d85048aeb3def61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[425,449]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />. Before this, Silvia must produce a number in the range <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/4/6c4ec6c90f7f9d147b6f37dab41f1cd4086899d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[213,224]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />. Before this, Bernardo must produce a number in the range <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/7/2c74fa588f22b763406a0347561206cc531f389b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[163,174]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />. Before this, Silvia must produce a number in the range <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/0/b701bcc3d868f98630f9b05eab2c5406a46b0b01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[82,87]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" />. Before this, Bernardo must produce a number in the range <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/7/eb7e9ad6309143501a3d157879690716fd251d2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[32,37]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" />. Before this, Silvia must produce a number in the range <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/e/82ea496e66a2dede47a10899b472c310d31ff34e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[16,18]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" />. Silvia could not have added 50 to any number before this to obtain a number in the range <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/e/82ea496e66a2dede47a10899b472c310d31ff34e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[16,18]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" />, hence the minimum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is 16 with the sum of digits being <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/b/7dbf74dc64cf0f4fb1e277e03bf74c5a8dff3880.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ 7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>If our first number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/6/35672a19103f2ead1f02935bb8450addc3318b94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"19\" height=\"16\" /> then the sequence of numbers will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/d/ffde9877dcef098fe8f38621d9042cece360806e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2N,~2N+50,~4N+100,~4N+150,~8N+300,~8N+350,~16N+700,~16N+750\\]\" width=\"584\" height=\"16\" /> Note that we cannot go any further because doubling gives an extra <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/6/726ceb374a9997197b7c47009e586ebf30a3d9a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1500$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> at the end, which is already greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/4/6b434ebc2071e706df740975a3c90aad3cfa1455.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"39\" height=\"13\" /> The smallest <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> will be given if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/c/a1c6263957c3a5575f9bdfc622ce28ed5c55ee60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16N+750&gt;1000&gt;16N+700 \\implies 15&lt;N&lt;19.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"411\" height=\"16\" /> Since the problem asks for the smallest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/6/35672a19103f2ead1f02935bb8450addc3318b94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"19\" height=\"16\" /> we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/b/e4bb513e21508306b77c013aae74e9c4b165e9fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" /> and the sum of its digits is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/c/16c3f53b077e4bd1c25a9b90219ffddee8c142b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+6=\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}~7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"120\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>~ 1001\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>If Bernardo is to win, he must produce a number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/8/1287b923c6098af91742b3832545c99b9049b205.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 950$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"16\" />. This would mean Silvia would have to hand him a number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/4/48481f95558b50b9353c4299fd901bc455dabcfd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r \\geq \\frac{950}{2}=475$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"118\" height=\"38\" />. This means Bernardo would have to give Silvia a number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/d/a5d8e36b0844d5a70a75c27892b162fa9dfff79e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s \\geq 475-50=425$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"154\" height=\"16\" />. Repeating this process gives the following sequence: \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/1/ee16db570c041032505cde65296ce3393c2b342a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[B=213, S=163, B=82, S=32, B=16\\]\" width=\"330\" height=\"16\" /> Thus, the smallest possible value is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/5/af55fdc1796e0249d2d7e12cd9676ce0b774c483.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+6=\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"116\" height=\"30\" />\n</p>\n<ul><li>Note: For all the values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, we always round up a value if the inequality gives a fraction, since we're using the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/c/3fcc68282472210e12994911b95ee7aa9c131856.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\geq$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" />                inequality.</li></ul>\n<p>~pandapower24\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B\">2012 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"20